Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  Description "What each member of the company makes of Carth and Gaunt by what they are: the cleric at the dead man's hands, the ranger in the Bishop's Wood, the thief in Heb's cellar, the mage at the planed-off plinth, the bard at the Fat Lamb. And the things only a particular calling can do: read the first leaf of the Register in the old rubric, and decide who to tell; face the Bishop's Wood at dusk.".

  // The preset party is not a set of declared people, so it has no Remarks of its own. What a rule can ask of a member
  // is their calling, and print their name. Said once for the company, by whoever it has of the calling.
  Relation heardByre(group). Relation heardDeadfall(group). Relation heardHeb(group). Relation heardPlinth(group). Relation heardLamb(group).

  // ── Act II, Carth: the cleric at the byre ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_byre at carth_byre when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_cleric) and awake(?m) and at(party, carth_byre) and not ralphLaid(carth_vigil) and not heardByre(party)
    says "{?m} stands over the hurdle and looks, for a long time, at the dead man's hands. 'Folded two ways,' {?m} says, very low, 'and slept with, and folded again. Somebody has been keeping him from going.' A pause. 'A man who is kept is not at peace. He is waiting. I have seen what that does to the one who keeps him.' {?m} does not look at the old woman on the stool. 'I could say the words. It would be a kindness to somebody. I do not know which of them it would be a kindness to.'" {
    Assert heardByre(party).
  }

  // ── Act III, the Bishop's Wood: the ranger ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_deadfall at deadfall when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_ranger) and awake(?m) and at(party, deadfall) and not heardDeadfall(party)
    says "{?m} goes along the edge of the clearing with a hand out, not touching. 'All in the same prints,' {?m} says. 'Five of them, and not one has put a foot down on its own.' {?m} straightens. 'They have a road, in a wood where no wolf has been given one. I should be out of here by four.'" {
    Assert heardDeadfall(party).
  }

  // ── Act III, the Row: the thief in Heb's cellar ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_heb at heb_cellar when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_thief) and awake(?m) and at(party, heb_cellar) and not heardHeb(party)
    says "{?m} takes a tally from the nearest bundle and tilts it to the lamp. 'Cut yesterday, smoked, rubbed with ash and mutton fat,' {?m} says. 'Whoever sold you one of these knew the Assessor looks at the ends and not at the notches.' A shrug. 'It's good work. It would be better if it were not the same work for the Fabric's accounts.'" {
    Assert heardHeb(party).
  }

  // ── Act IV, the Minster: the mage and the plinth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery plinth_lines "Five lines were dressed off the plinth of Saint Oswy's shrine by a different hand than cut the three that remain, perhaps a hundred years after them; the stone has not forgotten the depth of the letters.".
  Rule voice_plinth at minster_nave when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) and awake(?m) and at(party, minster_nave) and not ashDay() and not heardPlinth(party)
    says "{?m} runs two fingers across the dressed-back place on Oswy's plinth with the grain of the chisel. 'Five lines,' {?m} says. 'Not three. A stone remembers the depth of a letter the way a bruise remembers a hand.' The fingers come away. 'This was done later than the cutting by a hundred years, and by someone who was careful. It was not defaced. It was edited.'" teaches plinth_lines {
    Assert heardPlinth(party).
  }

  // ── Act IV, Fastens' Eve: the bard and the missing verse ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rule voice_lamb at fat_lamb when memberOf(?m, party) and hasCalling(?m, calling_bard) and awake(?m) and at(party, fat_lamb) and licence() and not heardLamb(party)
    says "{?m} sits with a cup untouched and an ear turned to the fiddle and the drum. 'Every song in this room has had the same verse taken out of it,' {?m} says. 'You can hear the gap. It is like a stair that is not there: everyone puts a foot down for it and takes a half-step.' A smile that does not stay. 'Somebody a long time ago asked the whole city to stop singing the same eight bars, and it did.'" {
    Assert heardLamb(party).
  }

  // ── The first leaf of the Register: the calling-unique reading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The Register's first book opens with a line every clerk in the Penitentiary can read. Under it, the original goes on
  // for nine lines in the rubric the Minster stopped teaching two hundred years ago, which every clerk copies, letter by
  // letter, at the head of each new book, and not one has read. A cleric can read it. Nobody else in Gaunt can, and no
  // one will have asked.
  Discovery first_leaf "Under the first line of the Register, the original goes on for nine lines in the old rubric: In the year the Bishop went away, the Penitentiary took up his keys, to keep and not to have, until they be asked for. Thirty-two keys are named; thirty-one were received. The Minster is of two towers, whereof the one shall carry the bell and the other the light, when it is asked for. To the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever. At the foot, cut small: a fish, and over it a flame.".
  Action read_first_leaf(actor: group, site: place, m: member) "Have {m} read the first leaf of the Register in the old rubric, under the clerks' copy" {
    Description "The clerks copy it at the head of every new book and not one of them has read it. It is nine lines. It will take an hour at the lectern with the Lady Penitentiary looking up from her desk.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, penitentiary) and daytime() and memberOf(m, actor) and hasCalling(m, calling_cleric) and awake(m) and not knows(actor, first_leaf).
    Time 6.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, first_leaf). }
    Result "{m} stands at the first lectern with a finger under the rubric, and reads it a line at a time, under the breath, the way one reads a thing one has been taught as a boy and never needed. At her desk by the fire Dame Hawise has stopped writing. Nine lines. The year the Bishop went away: the keys, taken up to keep and not to have, until they be asked for. Thirty-two named; thirty-one received. A Minster of two towers, the one to carry the bell and the other the light, when it is asked for. To the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever. At the foot, cut small in the vellum before the ink went on, a fish and over it a flame. {m} reads the last word aloud, and nobody in the room moves. 'It does not say where he went,' {m} says. 'It does not say who is to ask.'".
  }
  Rule leaf_known at penitentiary when at(party, penitentiary) and knows(party, first_leaf) and not leafHeard(party)
    says "The clerks have stopped copying. Nobody in the Penitentiary has ever heard the rubric read aloud, and the sound of it in the long room, with forty books standing in the quiet, is like a step on a stair someone had forgotten was there." {
    Assert leafHeard(party).
  }
  Relation leafHeard(group). Relation leafUsed(group). Relation grantShown(group). Relation hawiseReadLeaf(group).

  // The choice. The cleric has read the leaf once. It can be used one way: it cannot be spent twice.
  Action grant_to_woodmen(actor: group, site: place) "Show the Wood-reeve's woodmen the Bishop's grant, as read in the Register: to the poor of Gaunt the fallen wood, for ever" {
    Description "It opens the wood by right and not by leave. It tells the Lady Penitentiary nothing.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, wood_edge) and at(woodmen, site) and able(woodmen) and knows(actor, first_leaf) and not leafUsed(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert leafUsed(actor). Assert grantShown(actor). Assert at(woodmen, limbo). }
    Result "You give them the nine lines as you read them, the rubric and then the plain, standing in the snow before the board on its post. The biggest of the woodmen listens with his billhook on his shoulder, and when you have finished he goes to the post and puts his hand on the old cut letters under the Wood-reeve's board, TO THE POOR OF GAUNT, THE FALLEN WOOD, FOR EVER, as if they had just that moment appeared. 'I knew that,' he says, in an odd voice. 'My father said. I never knew it was wrote.' The three of them go back into the holly without another word, and do not come out. Nobody has told Thackray. Nobody has told the Lady.".
  }
  Action leaf_to_hawise(actor: group, site: place) "Lay the nine lines of the first leaf before Dame Hawise, as the Bishop wrote them" {
    Description "It tells the Lady Penitentiary what her keys are for. It opens nothing at the Wood.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, penitentiary) and at(hawise, penitentiary) and not masked(hawise) and knows(actor, first_leaf) and not leafUsed(actor) and not hawiseReadLeaf(hawise).
    Time 3.
    On success { Assert leafUsed(actor). Assert hawiseReadLeaf(hawise). Increase hawiseReasons(hawise) by 1. }
    Result "Dame Hawise listens with her pen laid across the page. When you have finished she gets up, and unhooks the billet of keys from her belt, and counts them aloud on the desk, one by one, in the voice of the Row, which she uses when she is frightened. 'Thirty-one,' she says. 'I have counted them every Michaelmas for eleven years, and never once asked why a Lady carries thirty-one of a thing whose first line is a number.' She puts them in your hand. 'Try them,' says the Lady Penitentiary, 'if you can think where.' You cannot. She takes them back. 'To keep and not to have,' she says. 'I have been had, by these, for eleven years. I have been so busy turning vanity into bread.' She sits down. 'Thank you. I do not know yet for what.'".
  }
  Rule fate_grant when accounting() and grantShown(party) and not spread(fate_grant)
    says "Of the Bishop's Wood: nobody knows who told the woodmen. They have stopped asking for four shillings, and keep the board on its post face inward, and the Row's children go out with their sledges on any afternoon they like, singing, and come back with the dead oak a sled at a time." {
    Assert spread(fate_grant).
  }
  Entity fate_grant: fact "the grant".
  Rule fate_leaf_hawise when accounting() and hawiseReadLeaf(hawise) and not spread(fate_leaf)
    says "Dame Hawise has had the nine lines copied out, in the plain, and hung beside the first lectern in the Penitentiary, where the clerks read them going past and do not know what to do with them. She has not decided what the thirty-second key is for. She says she is in no hurry to be asked." {
    Assert spread(fate_leaf).
  }
  Entity fate_leaf: fact "the leaf".

  // ── The Bishop's Wood at dusk: danger, and two ways that are not a fight ──────────────────────────────────────────
  // Five wolves, in the same prints, at the deadfall from four until seven. They can be fought, and it will cost. They can
  // be gone round, downwind, by someone who knows how; or sung at, in the Row's children's way, loud and slow, by
  // someone who has the end of the rhyme.
  Relation wolvesTurned(place).
  Rule wolves_rest when hour(clock) == 7 and wolvesTurned(deadfall) { Retract wolvesTurned(deadfall). }
  Relation wolvesRounded(group). Relation wolvesSung(group).
  Action round_deadfall(actor: group, site: place) "Take the company and the sledge wide round the wolves, downwind, along the bank of the beck" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deadfall) and at(wolves, site) and able(wolves) and capable(actor, woodcraft) and not wolvesRounded(actor).
    Time 3.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert wolvesRounded(actor). Assert wolvesTurned(deadfall). Assert at(wolves, limbo). Retract assails(wolves, actor). Retract warned(wolves, actor). }
    On failure { Assert wolvesRounded(actor). }
    Result "You wet a finger and hold it up, and go off the woodmen's path onto the bank of the beck where the hazel stands in the snow, with the wind coming at you off the wolves, rank, like a wet dog in a hot room. You go slowly. The biggest lifts her head as you pass, and holds it there, and you do not look at her. Half a mile on you come out on the track with the sledge and everyone you started with, and behind you in the dusk five grey shapes are going in single file along the other bank, in the same prints, toward Gaunt, and then not toward it.".
    Otherwise "Halfway round, the wind goes round, as it does in a wood at dusk, and the biggest lifts her head, and stands, and turns to look at you; and the rest stand up one after another, as if the snow had made them.".
  }
  Action sing_the_wolves(actor: group, site: place) "Sing the Row's sliding rhyme at them, to the end: loud, slow, and walking out" {
    Description "The Row's children go into the Bishop's Wood singing, because their mothers told them wolves do not care for a tune that has an end.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, deadfall) and at(wolves, site) and able(wolves) and knows(actor, second_verse) and not wolvesSung(actor).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, performance, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert wolvesSung(actor). Assert wolvesTurned(deadfall). Assert at(wolves, limbo). Retract assails(wolves, actor). Retract warned(wolves, actor). }
    On failure { Assert wolvesSung(actor). }
    Result "Oswy, Oswy, up the hill, you sing, loud and slow and a little flat, walking toward them with the sledge-rope in your fist; carry me and carry me still. The biggest tilts her head. At the top he set him down, you sing, and the wolves, one by one, sit, like dogs outside a butcher's; and on NOW WALK, said Oswy, into town the leader gets up, and turns her back on you, and goes, and the others after her, in the same prints, unhurried, as if it had been their idea.".
    Otherwise "You sing it, and your voice breaks on the second line, and the biggest of them hears the break and lowers her head.".
  }
}
